-- title:
--   Twin maximal orders at a prime dividing the level
-- statement:
--   Let $\bar r$ be a prime and $N$ a nonzero natural number with $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. Let $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that the quaternion algebra $H = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt` at $\bar r$, i.e. $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ every nonzero element of $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $\bar r$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda_1, R_1 \subseteq H$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (an order in the sense of containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and finitely generated, and maximal among such orders containing it), with $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders, the relative index of $R_1$ in the first being $N$), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$; let also $\Lambda_{1}^{s}$ be a maximal order with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1^s$ and $\Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_1^s = R_1$. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $N$ and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $\ell$. Then there are a ring isomorphism $\varphi : H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v \xrightarrow{\sim} M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and an $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ such that $\varphi(1 \otimes c) = c \cdot 1$ for all $c \in \mathbb{Q}_v$, and such that, writing $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ for the additive subgroup of $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$: an element $x$ lies in $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1\,v$ if and only if all entries of $h^{-1}\varphi(x)h$ lie in the valuation ring, and $x$ lies in $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1^s\,v$ if and only if all entries of $\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell^{-1})\,h^{-1}\varphi(x)h\,\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell)$ lie in the valuation ring.
--
--   This is the local description, at a prime $\ell$ exactly dividing the level, of a pair of maximal orders whose intersection is a given Eichler order of squarefree level $N$: in one common matrix frame the first completes to $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$ and the second to its $\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell)$-conjugate, so that the Eichler order completes to the Iwahori order. It is used in the study of the involution exchanging the twin pair, namely by [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_mem_forall_pow_smul_star_mul_mul_ne_smul_of_forall_pow_smul_mul_mul_star_ne_smul_of_inf_eq_of_dvd`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_mem_forall_pow_smul_star_mul_mul_ne_smul_of_forall_pow_smul_mul_mul_star_ne_smul_of_inf_eq_of_dvd) and [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.forall_exists_pow_smul_star_mul_mul_eq_smul_of_forall_pow_smul_mul_mul_star_ne_smul_of_inf_eq_of_dvd`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.forall_exists_pow_smul_star_mul_mul_eq_smul_of_forall_pow_smul_mul_mul_star_ne_smul_of_inf_eq_of_dvd).
